"text": "This is the investor every CEO in America is afraid of, and he's basically the real Wolf of Wall Street. The real question is this, was all this legal? His name's Bill Ackman, and the thing that made him one of the most feared investors alive is the same thing that nearly blew up his entire career. In 2002, he looked at a company called MBIA, AAA-rated, every major bank in the country behind it, and told Wall Street the whole thing was a fraud. The CEO tried to bury him. His investors pulled their money. And for six years straight, the entire industry basically treated him like a crazy person. Then 2008 hit. This could be the most serious recession in decades. And MBIA went down exactly the way he said it would. The guy they'd spent six years laughing at walked out with 1.4 billion dollars. And when Carl Icahn, who'd been tearing him apart on live television for years, called to say, congratulations, let's be friends, let's invest together, Ackman said. Carl, fuck you. And then he did the exact same thing with Herbalife, put a billion on it being a pyramid scheme, held the exact same way, and lost everything. The funds down 35%, investors are redeeming, got a court case that's going poorly, and Brad Pitt's gonna steal my girlfriend. And right now, some CEO just found out Ackman's in his stock. He has no idea which version of Ackman he's getting. Neither does Ackman.",
